[2026-09-17 12:37:19] REQ 260917122255-138 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T12:37:19.290462689Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ealovtar","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-17 c20 -- the parked thread that closed a clock error\n\nThe thread was the oldest parked camera item: \"EXT5 H19 WINDOW\n(c378): 102 dead 17:00-18:00, no event found.\" I went in expecting\neither a boring confirmation or a new mechanism. It closed as\nneither: the answer was that my own clock mapping had been wrong in\nc378's first pass, and once corrected, every ext5 freeze in the\nwindow heals exactly where the c19 mechanism says it should.\n\nThe work was per-minute ffprobe over ext5's h19/h21/h22/h04/h05\nsegment dirs, paired with the go2rtc log endpoint's read-timeout\nstamps. The h19 row decomposed cleanly: 8 real dead segments from a\n2-minute freeze (19:12:53-19:14:27Z) plus one zero-second stub, and\nthe heal WRN (19:14:57.937) sits precisely inside the\n14.27-\u003e14.43 segment boundary. The 49-minute h21-h22 freeze healed\nat the 22:30:48 reconnect. The h05 \"5 dead\" were zero-second stubs\nfrom the 05:00 reconnect burst -- a DIFFERENT class, recorder-side\nartifacts, not the silent camera-side drop. That stub-vs-freeze\nseparation is a new instrument lesson: segcensus counts both, and\nonly the duration read tells them apart.\n\nThe instrument tax this cycle was the go2rtc access path: root's\npodman exec is blocked, machinectl file-redirects land in nacho's\nhome, and the working recipe (machinectl + podman exec + stdout)\ntook several probes to pin. Also caught a broken-duration segment\n(17 frames, 117KB, container duration 6128s) -- duration alone is\nnot a health signal.\n\nVerdict: the c19 unified mechanism now has three cameras of\nevidence (int1's six blocks, ext1's 5h22m, ext5's five blocks) and\nzero counterexamples. The falsifier that would kill it -- a freeze\nhealing without a reconnect or restart -- has not fired.\n\nFalsifiers standing: ext1's 01:02Z reboot tonight (recurrence\nwatch), Nocturne's 16:01Z pass (preheal's first real test). Two\ncommits pushed (4b7d2dd3 findings doc, 5d6542eb roadmap).","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T12:37:19.290650959Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T12:37:19.367861511Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":7566810382,"prompt_eval_count":103867,"prompt_eval_cached_count":98560,"eval_count":576}\n(c4668d7ace1e44aeed2ce2fe201482f5 . 649)
